1
00:00:07,470 --> 00:00:10,310
Ji Won Ho, you can do an alteration right now, can't you?

2
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:11,940
An alteration? Here?

3
00:00:12,110 --> 00:00:13,210
What are you talking about?

4
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:15,750
The finale is going on as planned.

5
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:17,380
How? We don't have a model.

6
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,750
I'm doing it.

7
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:21,050
What?

8
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:26,790
Ji Won Ho. I'm giving you ten minutes.

9
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:49,350
Hurry. We're out of time.

10
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:51,950
All right.

11
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,640
And now for tonight's highlight.

12
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,740
Our finale model makes her entrance.

13
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,220
Brava.

14
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,940
(Episode 4)

15
00:02:57,710 --> 00:02:59,310
- That was a great performance. - You were absolutely radiant.

16
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:00,380
I really enjoyed the show.

17
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,010
- Thank you for coming. - Truly the best.

18
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,180
- It was so beautiful. - That dress is gorgeous, isn't it?

19
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:05,480
- Isn't it? Thank you. - Yes.

20
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,820
Please, have some champagne.

21
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,150
- Okay. - You all worked so hard today.

22
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:12,260
- Have a wonderful time. - Okay.

23
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:21,700
- He says it was a fantastic finale. - Thank you.

24
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,630
Please tell him it was an honour for me...

25
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:24,800
to work with Bruni, too.

26
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,940
Thank you. It was an honour for me, too.

27
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:30,170
Thanks to the collaboration with Bruni.

28
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:31,770
Thank you so much.

29
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:35,650
Ma'am, there's someone waiting for you outside.

30
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:38,950
- Sir, can we get a photo with you? - You were amazing.

31
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:40,020
Yes, thank you.

32
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,580
Sir, can we please get just one picture?

33
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:44,450
- Can you do a finger heart for us? - A finger heart?

34
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,490
Thank you for your hard work.

35
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,590
- You'll call us again next time? - Thank you.

36
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,690
- That's right. - Thank you.

37
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,960
- Thank you. - That was amazing.

38
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:52,500
- Thank you. - You're so cool.

39
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,560
Okay, thank you.

40
00:03:58,570 --> 00:03:59,570
Right this way.

41
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:13,680
You were amazing on stage today.

42
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:15,350
Congratulations, Mi Young.

43
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,130
I've always wondered what you'd look like...

44
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:25,700
in a dress,

45
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:28,430
and it was just as I imagined.

46
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:30,900
Really?

47
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:36,910
The dress I wore at my wedding was much more spectacular.

48
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,710
Now I'm grateful all over again.

49
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,680
For you leaving me back then.

50
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:48,520
I didn't know back then.

51
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:51,920
If I had known the truth beforehand,

52
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,760
I never would have let you go like that.

53
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:00,230
I'm sorry, Mi Young.

54
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:04,500
Hey, Calvin.

55
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,090
Don't even think about making a move on me like this.

56
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:27,790
I'm not the Baek Mi Young you once knew.

57
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,100
At this rate, I'll be taking pictures all night.

58
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,800
The corners of my mouth are twitching.

59
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:42,270
Have you seen the designer, Ji Won Ho?

60
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:44,440
I know. We have to get a picture with him...

61
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:46,310
for Instagram. Seriously, where did he go?

62
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,380
I know.

63
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:50,610
Hey, over there. Isn't that Designer Ji Won Ho?

64
00:05:51,210 --> 00:05:52,880
- Where? - Over there.

65
00:05:53,550 --> 00:05:56,190
- I think that's him. Let's go. - Let's go, come on.

66
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:57,550
I'm pretty sure that's him.

67
00:05:58,390 --> 00:05:59,360
Sir.

68
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:00,560
Over here, quick.

69
00:06:02,790 --> 00:06:04,460
- That is Designer Ji Won Ho. - Over here...

70
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:08,900
- That's weird. He was right here. - He's gone.

71
00:06:08,970 --> 00:06:09,970
No, really...

72
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:12,370
- I think he went that way. - Hey, over there...

73
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,440
Hey, over there.

74
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:26,180
I can finally breathe.

75
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,820
I know. It was so stuffy inside.

76
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,060
This is nice.

77
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:40,160
You didn't come out here because of me, did you?

78
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:45,870
Well, see you then.

79
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,200
Chicken and beer.

80
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,470
Buy me some.

81
00:06:52,710 --> 00:06:54,210
I said you should buy me some chicken and beer.

82
00:06:55,110 --> 00:06:56,280
You can do that much, right?

83
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:09,290
Excuse me. Another 500cc beer, please.

84
00:07:09,590 --> 00:07:11,690
Seriously? How much more are you planning to drink?

85
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,830
Why? Are you scared?

86
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:18,530
- What? - Don't worry. I don't get drunk.

87
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,140
But...

88
00:07:24,810 --> 00:07:26,010
what's the reason?

89
00:07:26,510 --> 00:07:30,580
- The reason? - You were the one who said it.

90
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:31,680
That I...

91
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:34,150
That you liked me...

92
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:38,450
The reason why I like you?

93
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:44,390
I couldn't forget it.

94
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:47,760
That warmth.

95
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:49,730
Warmth?

96
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:54,100
Eight years ago, what you said back then.

97
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:04,910
Now that it's come to this, you have no reason to stay here.

98
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,350
So, you want me to go back to Korea alone?

99
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,750
And if you don't?

100
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,820
What will you do? Just stay here and fight with your stepmother?

101
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,460
If you had talent, I would've kept supporting you.

102
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,160
It would've been uncomfortable, but I was going to...

103
00:08:21,230 --> 00:08:23,100
try and have the three of us live together.

104
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,100
Oh.

105
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:30,410
So I'm nothing to you now, Dad?

106
00:08:31,910 --> 00:08:33,110
Because I have no talent?

107
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:37,780
Don't feel so wronged. I've done my part as a father.

108
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:45,250
My stepmother was from Milan,

109
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:48,220
and she really hated me.

110
00:08:51,230 --> 00:08:54,260
My dad just walked on eggshells around me and my stepmother,

111
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:57,030
and in the end, he chose my stepmother.

112
00:08:58,270 --> 00:08:59,270
He abandoned me.

113
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:14,080
Excuse me, I'm just going to use the restroom.

114
00:09:14,150 --> 00:09:15,150
Of course, go ahead.

115
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,570
Where do you think you're going?

116
00:09:42,010 --> 00:09:44,450
Excuse me, you're Korean, right?

117
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,550
It's good to help others,

118
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:54,660
but you shouldn't lose your own valuables.

119
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:57,960
This seems much more valuable than my wallet.

120
00:10:05,870 --> 00:10:06,870
Hey...

121
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,440
It all passes.

122
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:16,110
Stay strong. It'll all pass eventually.

123
00:10:18,510 --> 00:10:19,520
But...

124
00:10:21,050 --> 00:10:22,620
what you said to me back then...

125
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:25,520
The words, "It all passes."

126
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:29,990
Those simple words felt so warm.

127
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:33,830
Because of what you said, I found my courage again.

128
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:37,000
The courage to do well on my own.

129
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,240
You must have gone through a lot.

130
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:43,670
I'm okay now.

131
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:47,240
Just like you said, it really did all pass.

132
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:50,850
I really just said it without thinking.

133
00:10:51,510 --> 00:10:55,280
Then was the last thing you said also without much thought?

134
00:10:56,250 --> 00:10:58,390
- What did I say? - You said...

135
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:00,860
that you were grateful I got back your wallet,

136
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:04,230
and that if we ever met again, you'd be sure to repay me.

137
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:06,960
I did say that.

138
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:09,670
I meant it. Of course, I have to repay you.

139
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:13,270
- Meet me just three times. - What?

140
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,840
From now on, exactly three times, whenever I want.

141
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:18,010
Let's meet up like this and just talk.

142
00:11:18,770 --> 00:11:20,380
That's how you can repay your debt.

143
00:11:22,450 --> 00:11:23,450
Really?

144
00:11:24,150 --> 00:11:25,380
That's all it would take?

145
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:27,950
Yes.

146
00:11:29,490 --> 00:11:30,520
Okay.

147
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:33,220
Cheers.

148
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:38,560
Don't you think this is fate?

149
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:42,570
I've prayed during every full moon since then.

150
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:44,930
I asked to see you again.

151
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:50,070
And now, here we are.

152
00:11:53,110 --> 00:11:55,240
- What is she talking about? - Excuse me.

153
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:56,910
Can I get another one over here?

154
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,820
You can order another one when you finish that.

155
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,490
I'm dying here.

156
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,160
But hey...

157
00:12:12,230 --> 00:12:14,030
How much have we had to drink?

158
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:18,030
Ten 500cc glasses each.

159
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,100
About 10,000cc?

160
00:12:22,470 --> 00:12:23,510
Oh my god.

161
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,540
Are you okay? You're not drunk?

162
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,980
I'm honestly fine.

163
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:32,880
I told you, I don't get drunk no matter how much I drink.

164
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,150
Gosh, you can really hold your liquor.

165
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:38,250
Other than my wife,

166
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:40,190
I've never met anyone who can drink so much.

167
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:45,090
I guess your wife can really drink too.

168
00:12:45,660 --> 00:12:48,460
She's an amazing drinker. Super tough.

169
00:12:49,130 --> 00:12:52,200
That's one of the things I fell for.

170
00:12:55,170 --> 00:12:56,470
And now,

171
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,770
do you love her?

172
00:13:01,810 --> 00:13:03,380
When you see your wife,

173
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,880
does your heart still flutter?

174
00:13:18,930 --> 00:13:21,260
Flutter? Why would it flutter?

175
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:23,730
Let's get going.

176
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,000
I can't drink anymore.

177
00:13:25,070 --> 00:13:26,140
Goodness.

178
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:53,730
(Jihwaja Motel)

179
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,930
Why are you following me?

180
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,700
Because I'm worried.

181
00:13:57,930 --> 00:14:00,370
- What? - On the way here,

182
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,610
do you know you almost fell three times?

183
00:14:03,610 --> 00:14:04,970
Right.

184
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:08,510
By any chance, do you live here?

185
00:14:09,350 --> 00:14:10,510
(Jihwaja Motel)

186
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,620
This is my place for now.

187
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:19,920
Anyway, I had fun. Take care.

188
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,470
CEO Ji.

189
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:34,640
(Jihwaja Motel)

190
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:44,380
Darn it.

191
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:01,300
CEO Ji?

192
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:03,970
CEO Ji.

193
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,340
We switched phones.

194
00:15:23,350 --> 00:15:25,390
Mi Young.

195
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,290
Mi Young.

196
00:15:45,610 --> 00:15:47,110
Hurry. We're out of time.

197
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,010
All right.

198
00:16:22,850 --> 00:16:24,710
(Husband)

199
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:27,920
Won Ho, you worked hard today.

200
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,560
Thanks for...

201
00:16:40,130 --> 00:16:41,130
Where...

202
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:42,930
are you?

203
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:48,840
(Husband)

204
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,910
(Mi Young)

205
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:05,020
The customer you are trying to reach is unavailable.

206
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,690
Please leave a message after the beep...

207
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:31,480
I knew it.

208
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:33,250
What did he take?

209
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,060
Mi Young.

210
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:44,090
Why did you call at this hour?

211
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:47,200
How are you, Seung Ho?

212
00:17:47,530 --> 00:17:49,570
Oh, you know me. I'm always doing great.

213
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:51,270
Are you doing all right, Mi Young?

214
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:55,870
Yes. The reason I'm calling is,

215
00:17:56,370 --> 00:17:58,070
is Won Ho,

216
00:17:58,710 --> 00:18:00,210
by any chance, at your mother's house?

217
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:03,880
Won Ho is staying at my motel right now.

218
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:06,320
The motel?

219
00:18:06,650 --> 00:18:08,750
You know how our mom is, Mi Young.

220
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:10,520
He can't possibly go home,

221
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:12,250
so he says he's more comfortable here.

222
00:18:12,890 --> 00:18:13,890
I see.

223
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:15,290
Mi Young.

224
00:18:15,790 --> 00:18:16,830
Speaking of which,

225
00:18:16,890 --> 00:18:19,330
could you come and drag that brat Won Ho home?

226
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,730
He's a complete mess these days.

227
00:18:23,930 --> 00:18:24,930
Well...

228
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,300
I'm sorry. This is all our fault.

229
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,510
Oh, you have nothing to be sorry for, Mi Young.

230
00:18:32,510 --> 00:18:34,180
Mi Young, I'm sorry, but some customers just arrived.

231
00:18:35,310 --> 00:18:37,650
- For an overnight stay? - No, just for a few hours.

232
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:39,050
Okay.

233
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,470
When he's sleeping,

234
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:02,700
he's kind of like a baby.

235
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,680
(Jihwaja Motel)

236
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:55,590
What a weird dream.

237
00:20:08,170 --> 00:20:09,770
What the?

238
00:20:11,270 --> 00:20:12,410
You're awake?

239
00:20:13,710 --> 00:20:16,240
Hey, what are you doing? Why are you here?

240
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:17,550
What?

241
00:20:17,610 --> 00:20:19,980
I'm asking why you were sleeping here, Hee Ju.

242
00:20:22,550 --> 00:20:25,350
It looks like we swapped phones yesterday.

243
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:28,260
I came to switch them back, and then...

244
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,660
And then?

245
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:32,090
I must've fallen asleep because I was so tired.

246
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,160
No matter how tired you were,

247
00:20:34,230 --> 00:20:35,830
how could you think of sleeping here?

248
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:38,930
- Are you crazy? - What can I do? I already slept.

249
00:20:39,130 --> 00:20:40,240
Want me to undo it?

250
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:43,640
Unbelievable.

251
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:44,970
Jeez.

252
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,440
Jeez.

253
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:51,110
Won Ho will be so touched.

254
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,850
Is that why you came so early in the morning?

255
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,280
To bring Won Ho a change of clothes?

256
00:20:55,650 --> 00:20:56,820
I noticed...

257
00:20:57,450 --> 00:20:59,520
he didn't pack any of his things.

258
00:21:00,090 --> 00:21:01,690
And I don't know when he'll be back.

259
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:04,190
Look, instead of all this,

260
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,160
why don't you two just make up now?

261
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,800
- What? - To be honest, Mi Young,

262
00:21:09,870 --> 00:21:11,870
you don't really want a divorce either, right?

263
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:14,670
If you really couldn't stand Won Ho, why would you bring him clothes?

264
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:17,470
Just a moment.

265
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:21,040
(Information)

266
00:21:21,740 --> 00:21:23,410
It's Room 304. Go on up.

267
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:26,950
- No, it's okay. Could you just... - No way.

268
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:28,680
Since you're the one who brought them,

269
00:21:28,950 --> 00:21:30,220
you should be the one to give them to him.

270
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:32,020
Go on.

271
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:34,760
Go on.

272
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:37,160
(Jihwaja Motel)

273
00:21:37,230 --> 00:21:38,290
Hurry up.

274
00:21:41,230 --> 00:21:42,230
Okay.

275
00:21:45,630 --> 00:21:46,900
Hee Ju, wait a second.

276
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:48,800
- Hold on. - Yes?

277
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:50,470
Are you just going to leave like that?

278
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:52,170
Well, how else should I leave?

279
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:54,840
No, what I mean is...

280
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:58,210
Wait.

281
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:01,680
About last night...

282
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:04,990
I didn't make any mistakes, did I?

283
00:22:06,990 --> 00:22:08,620
I'm just...

284
00:22:09,690 --> 00:22:11,060
checking, just in case.

285
00:22:12,090 --> 00:22:15,460
You didn't forget everything from last night, did you?

286
00:22:16,300 --> 00:22:17,300
What?

287
00:22:22,370 --> 00:22:24,010
We made a promise yesterday.

288
00:22:24,970 --> 00:22:25,970
A promise?

289
00:22:26,210 --> 00:22:27,710
That you'd meet me three times.

290
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:31,110
Yes, I remember that.

291
00:22:32,150 --> 00:22:33,180
Then we're good.

292
00:22:34,050 --> 00:22:35,880
Hee Ju, wait a second.

293
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:46,700
I'm sorry. I must have the wrong room.

294
00:22:47,930 --> 00:22:48,930
Hee Ju.

295
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,130
Let's just talk a little more, okay?

296
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:51,700
Darn it.

297
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:05,950
(Jihwaja Motel)

298
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:09,050
Mi Young, are you leaving already?

299
00:23:09,890 --> 00:23:10,990
And she's gone.

300
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,890
Hey, Won Ho.

301
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,060
Mi Young, wait.

302
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,320
Mi Young, wait a minute. Just listen to me.

303
00:23:16,390 --> 00:23:17,530
Just listen for a second.

304
00:23:19,060 --> 00:23:20,400
This is all a complete misunderstanding.

305
00:23:20,630 --> 00:23:22,700
It's absolutely not what you think.

306
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:26,030
What I think? And what is it that I'm thinking?

307
00:23:26,770 --> 00:23:28,040
No, I mean...

308
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:29,840
Hee Ju.

309
00:23:29,970 --> 00:23:31,670
Hee Ju, help me out here.

310
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,610
Nothing happened between us last night.

311
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:36,710
Right?

312
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:38,180
That's right.

313
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,950
Nothing happened between me and CEO Ji.

314
00:23:42,950 --> 00:23:45,590
CEO Ji and I just had some drinks,

315
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,060
and since we were tired, we slept together, that's all.

316
00:23:48,590 --> 00:23:49,660
Right.

317
00:23:52,690 --> 00:23:55,100
Wait, what do you mean by that? "Slept together?"

318
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:57,200
Well, we did sleep in the same room.

319
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:01,940
No.

320
00:24:02,570 --> 00:24:03,770
(Jihwaja Motel)

321
00:24:06,040 --> 00:24:07,040
I see.

322
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:09,540
Then you two can just keep getting along in one room.

323
00:24:13,250 --> 00:24:14,480
No, Mi Young.

324
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:17,120
It's not like that.

325
00:24:20,260 --> 00:24:21,420
Darn it.

326
00:24:28,930 --> 00:24:31,100
This is just perfect.

327
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,840
Verbal abuse, profanity, assault, neglect,

328
00:24:33,900 --> 00:24:36,870
and, to top it off, adultery.

329
00:24:36,940 --> 00:24:39,140
Now you've finally checked all the boxes.

330
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:42,480
Stop it. I'm not in the mood for jokes.

331
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:45,080
Jokes? I'm just stating the facts.

332
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:47,620
How could something like this happen?

333
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:49,750
All I did was go to sleep and wake up.

334
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:52,290
Lawyer, what do I do now?

335
00:24:52,350 --> 00:24:53,320
What do you think?

336
00:24:53,390 --> 00:24:57,690
- Get ready for the nuclear bomb. - A nuclear bomb?

337
00:24:58,630 --> 00:25:00,000
That's why a man must always...

338
00:25:00,060 --> 00:25:02,600
be wary of women and alcohol.

339
00:25:02,660 --> 00:25:03,730
But at the very time...

340
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,700
you should have been most cautious,

341
00:25:06,470 --> 00:25:07,870
you went and slept with her.

342
00:25:08,670 --> 00:25:09,670
Slept with her?

343
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:11,240
I'm telling you, this is completely unfair.

344
00:25:11,310 --> 00:25:12,870
Strictly speaking,

345
00:25:13,210 --> 00:25:15,840
it was a twin bedroom...

346
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:20,020
We have to send our response soon,

347
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:23,720
and you picked the perfect time to get into trouble.

348
00:25:30,990 --> 00:25:32,890
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

349
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:50,450
I'm sorry. I must have the wrong room.

350
00:25:51,580 --> 00:25:54,450
Hee Ju. Let's just talk a little more, okay?

351
00:25:56,350 --> 00:25:59,320
CEO Ji and I just had some drinks,

352
00:25:59,750 --> 00:26:01,690
and since we were tired, we slept together, that's all.

353
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:29,450
Mi Young, do you want some cof...

354
00:26:38,260 --> 00:26:39,630
It was like...

355
00:26:39,690 --> 00:26:42,960
the calm before the storm, you know?

356
00:26:43,470 --> 00:26:45,770
No, Mi Young's expression was just like...

357
00:26:45,830 --> 00:26:49,640
Yi Sun Sin right before heading into battle.

358
00:26:49,740 --> 00:26:51,310
Come on, Director Song. How would you know...

359
00:26:51,370 --> 00:26:52,940
what General Yi Sun Sin's expression was?

360
00:26:53,010 --> 00:26:57,080
It was a figure of speech. Oh, honestly.

361
00:26:59,380 --> 00:27:01,080
I wonder what's wrong.

362
00:27:01,750 --> 00:27:05,950
Yesterday's show went well, and everyone was in a good mood.

363
00:27:07,690 --> 00:27:09,120
Do you think she and CEO Ji...

364
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:11,430
fought again on the way home yesterday?

365
00:27:12,090 --> 00:27:14,360
Whatever's going on between them is their business.

366
00:27:14,560 --> 00:27:16,630
You shouldn't get so involved, Director Song.

367
00:27:16,730 --> 00:27:18,900
When have I ever gotten involved?

368
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:21,300
Come on. You do it every day.

369
00:27:21,370 --> 00:27:23,640
You're always next to CEO Baek like a little sparrow,

370
00:27:23,710 --> 00:27:25,540
chirping away.

371
00:27:26,810 --> 00:27:28,140
A sparrow?

372
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:29,580
The nerve.

373
00:27:30,150 --> 00:27:33,210
You want me to really show you how to peck?

374
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:35,080
I'll show you a sparrow. Chirp, chirp, chirp.

375
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:37,620
- What are you doing? Hey, stop. - Chirp, chirp, chirp.

376
00:27:37,690 --> 00:27:39,020
What do you think you're doing?

377
00:27:39,320 --> 00:27:40,790
Chirp, chirp, chirp...

378
00:27:51,330 --> 00:27:53,200
Of all the times for her to show up.

379
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:57,010
She brought me some clothes.

380
00:27:57,510 --> 00:28:00,140
She usually doesn't care what I wear or eat,

381
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:02,280
but of all days, why did she have to come today? Darn it.

382
00:28:02,340 --> 00:28:04,750
Then why, out of all the days you could have picked,

383
00:28:04,810 --> 00:28:06,550
did you choose to have an affair yesterday?

384
00:28:06,610 --> 00:28:08,950
The day before your wife was set to barge in.

385
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:10,950
I told you, it wasn't an affair. I swear.

386
00:28:11,020 --> 00:28:13,320
Okay. Then let me correct that with the proper legal term.

387
00:28:13,390 --> 00:28:14,390
Adultery.

388
00:28:14,590 --> 00:28:15,620
Adul...

389
00:28:16,590 --> 00:28:18,390
Seriously... Darn it.

390
00:28:19,430 --> 00:28:20,430
Lawyer, does this mean...

391
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:22,800
I just have to go along with whatever my wife wants...

392
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,730
and let her divorce me?

393
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:26,770
Well, we can try to come up with an explanation,

394
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:29,800
but the fact is, this puts us at a huge disadvantage.

395
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:33,140
Not unless their side messes up even bigger than we did.

396
00:28:33,810 --> 00:28:36,880
Not a chance. My wife is incredibly meticulous.

397
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:38,010
Then you'd better be...

398
00:28:38,710 --> 00:28:42,320
on your best behaviour. From this moment on,

399
00:28:42,420 --> 00:28:44,020
don't even think about playing with fire.

400
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:47,420
Whether you're awake or asleep, watch out for fire.

401
00:28:47,790 --> 00:28:48,890
Watch out for fire.

402
00:28:55,830 --> 00:28:57,100
Kyung Tae.

403
00:28:59,030 --> 00:29:00,030
What?

404
00:29:00,770 --> 00:29:02,200
Who did you say came to the office?

405
00:29:05,510 --> 00:29:08,510
Our hotel is celebrating its 40th anniversary this year.

406
00:29:09,310 --> 00:29:11,010
For our senior clientele,

407
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:14,050
we're thinking of holding a vow renewal event,

408
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:17,320
and we'd love for J&White to collaborate with us.

409
00:29:17,950 --> 00:29:20,290
Since it's our 40th anniversary event,

410
00:29:20,390 --> 00:29:23,990
the promotional benefit will be huge for us, and for J&White as well.

411
00:29:24,190 --> 00:29:27,100
The studio, the dresses, the makeup...

412
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:29,630
All the costs for the entire event...

413
00:29:29,700 --> 00:29:31,100
We'll cover everything.

414
00:29:32,630 --> 00:29:35,770
But why are you so set on doing this with us?

415
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:37,740
Do I really have to say?

416
00:29:43,610 --> 00:29:46,410
Right. If you work with me,

417
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:48,150
I'm sure your husband would find it awkward.

418
00:29:50,550 --> 00:29:52,990
So, think about it and let me know.

419
00:29:57,260 --> 00:29:59,060
Nothing happened between us last night.

420
00:29:59,130 --> 00:30:00,500
Right?

421
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:03,700
CEO Ji and I just had some drinks,

422
00:30:03,770 --> 00:30:05,900
and since we were tired, we slept together, that's all.

423
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:10,640
All right.

424
00:30:11,870 --> 00:30:13,270
I don't see why not.

425
00:30:15,010 --> 00:30:16,180
On second thought,

426
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:18,110
I think this is a good opportunity for us too.

427
00:30:18,850 --> 00:30:20,380
Let's do it. The collaboration.

428
00:30:29,590 --> 00:30:30,630
It's important.

429
00:30:36,560 --> 00:30:37,800
That's right.

430
00:30:50,610 --> 00:30:51,850
Hello, CEO Ji.

431
00:30:53,310 --> 00:30:56,780
It's an honour to be working with you again.

432
00:30:56,850 --> 00:30:58,120
Excuse me?

433
00:30:58,650 --> 00:31:00,690
He's just a business partner.

434
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:04,990
You heard from the vice president, didn't you?

435
00:31:05,260 --> 00:31:07,700
This collaboration with the Calvin Hotel...

436
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,500
is an opportunity we have absolutely...

437
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:10,600
no reason to turn down.

438
00:31:10,700 --> 00:31:12,070
What do you mean there's no reason to turn it down?

439
00:31:12,130 --> 00:31:13,430
For one thing, I haven't approved it.

440
00:31:13,430 --> 00:31:15,000
Whether it's Calvin or not.

441
00:31:15,070 --> 00:31:18,910
- Should've discussed it with me. - And you.

442
00:31:18,970 --> 00:31:20,280
Did you discuss it with me before you went...

443
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:21,440
to a motel and slept with that girl?

444
00:31:21,540 --> 00:31:22,540
What?

445
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,280
Hey, I already made myself clear.

446
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:27,520
I'm telling you, nothing like that happened. Really.

447
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:30,890
And Hee Ju and I...

448
00:31:30,950 --> 00:31:33,050
We don't have the kind of relationship you think we do.

449
00:31:33,150 --> 00:31:35,590
Not that kind of relationship? Then what is it?

450
00:31:37,330 --> 00:31:38,330
Well...

451
00:31:39,330 --> 00:31:41,430
Someone who provided comfort in moments of struggle?

452
00:31:41,460 --> 00:31:42,860
Goodness me.

453
00:31:42,900 --> 00:31:44,470
What kind of great comfort was she planning on giving you...

454
00:31:44,530 --> 00:31:45,970
that you had to go to a motel?

455
00:31:46,030 --> 00:31:48,270
Gosh, you always have to put it like that...

456
00:31:48,340 --> 00:31:50,510
Anyway, about working with Calvin,

457
00:31:50,570 --> 00:31:52,270
discuss it with me again before you decide.

458
00:31:52,570 --> 00:31:53,680
No.

459
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:56,140
I'm not changing my mind. I'm just going to do it.

460
00:31:56,310 --> 00:31:57,310
What?

461
00:31:57,850 --> 00:32:01,020
As the CEO of this company, I simply made a rational decision.

462
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:04,150
The employees agreed without any objections. So...

463
00:32:04,220 --> 00:32:06,450
don't even think about ruining this, and just follow my lead.

464
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:10,330
Who are you telling to follow your lead? Am I your dog?

465
00:32:11,290 --> 00:32:12,430
Oh, right.

466
00:32:12,490 --> 00:32:14,560
You don't have much time left to submit your response.

467
00:32:14,630 --> 00:32:15,800
Don't miss the deadline.

468
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:21,240
Unbelievable...

469
00:32:23,100 --> 00:32:24,910
It's revenge, that's what it is.

470
00:32:25,540 --> 00:32:26,540
Revenge?

471
00:32:26,610 --> 00:32:28,710
"How dare you go in and out of a motel with another woman?"

472
00:32:29,110 --> 00:32:32,050
"Fine, then I'll go ahead and work with my ex-boyfriend."

473
00:32:32,610 --> 00:32:33,720
"As of today,"

474
00:32:33,780 --> 00:32:35,780
"I will walk the path of the office wife."

475
00:32:36,950 --> 00:32:39,420
- Something like that. - What? An office wife?

476
00:32:39,650 --> 00:32:41,220
I'm just kidding.

477
00:32:41,890 --> 00:32:45,130
I really shouldn't have drunk so much yesterday.

478
00:32:45,260 --> 00:32:46,260
But...

479
00:32:46,430 --> 00:32:48,230
are you sure nothing happened?

480
00:32:50,200 --> 00:32:52,400
You said you completely blacked out.

481
00:32:52,730 --> 00:32:54,840
If by some chance something did happen yesterday...

482
00:32:54,900 --> 00:32:57,110
Nothing. Absolutely nothing.

483
00:32:57,470 --> 00:32:58,570
Hey, no matter how drunk I get,

484
00:32:58,640 --> 00:33:00,040
I would never make that kind of mistake.

485
00:33:00,110 --> 00:33:01,380
I may not be perfect, but when it comes to women,

486
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:02,880
you know I have nothing to hide, don't you?

487
00:33:02,940 --> 00:33:05,450
I know. I know better than anyone...

488
00:33:05,510 --> 00:33:06,850
that you're clean when it comes to women.

489
00:33:06,910 --> 00:33:07,920
Darn it...

490
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:10,080
Anyway, if Baek Mi Young uses this as an excuse...

491
00:33:10,150 --> 00:33:11,850
to try something with that jerk Calvin,

492
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:13,420
I swear I won't just let it slide.

493
00:33:14,220 --> 00:33:15,290
And what if you don't?

494
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:18,460
- What? - Will you pick a fight with Calvin?

495
00:33:18,590 --> 00:33:21,000
If I have to, I'll do more than just fight him.

496
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:46,990
And Hee Ju and I...

497
00:33:47,020 --> 00:33:49,090
We don't have the kind of relationship you think we do.

498
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:51,730
Not that kind of relationship? Then what is it?

499
00:33:51,930 --> 00:33:52,930
Well...

500
00:33:53,730 --> 00:33:55,860
Someone who provided comfort in moments of struggle?

501
00:34:30,700 --> 00:34:33,400
So, Baek Mi Young left here first.

502
00:34:34,470 --> 00:34:36,340
And Won Ho followed right after her.

503
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:41,310
But what on earth is this?

504
00:34:44,050 --> 00:34:45,050
Hey.

505
00:34:45,150 --> 00:34:46,550
What are you doing?

506
00:34:48,850 --> 00:34:50,590
Lining up all these drinks.

507
00:34:51,020 --> 00:34:53,520
Mom. Mi Young was here yesterday.

508
00:34:54,020 --> 00:34:55,290
Why was that sly fox here?

509
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:57,020
She'd brought Won Ho clothes and underwear.

510
00:34:57,890 --> 00:35:00,230
I guess she's still worried since he's her husband.

511
00:35:00,500 --> 00:35:01,500
But...

512
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,660
there was another woman besides Mi Young.

513
00:35:05,130 --> 00:35:06,200
What?

514
00:35:06,330 --> 00:35:07,340
Another woman? Who?

515
00:35:07,400 --> 00:35:08,670
I don't know who she was.

516
00:35:09,340 --> 00:35:10,370
But...

517
00:35:10,710 --> 00:35:12,340
that woman and Won Ho left together.

518
00:35:13,270 --> 00:35:14,540
The three of them left, including Mi Young.

519
00:35:14,880 --> 00:35:17,140
Try to make some sense.

520
00:35:17,280 --> 00:35:18,580
So you're saying the three of them...

521
00:35:18,650 --> 00:35:20,180
were at the motel together yesterday?

522
00:35:20,250 --> 00:35:21,820
Yes, that's what I'm saying.

523
00:35:22,350 --> 00:35:24,420
I don't get it at all either.

524
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:28,220
So there is another woman?

525
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:33,590
Oh, dear.

526
00:35:46,440 --> 00:35:47,440
Strange...

527
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:55,380
"Bae Su Ji?"

528
00:36:13,270 --> 00:36:15,170
You're very talented.

529
00:36:15,540 --> 00:36:16,540
I was very impressed with your work.

530
00:36:17,100 --> 00:36:21,410
Thank you. By the way, is CEO Ji not here?

531
00:36:22,980 --> 00:36:24,510
He's very busy today.

532
00:36:25,010 --> 00:36:26,210
That's why I'm here instead.

533
00:36:27,480 --> 00:36:28,480
I see.

534
00:36:54,140 --> 00:36:55,640
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

535
00:36:58,010 --> 00:36:59,050
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

536
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:04,690
From this moment on,

537
00:37:04,690 --> 00:37:06,090
don't even think about playing with fire.

538
00:37:06,290 --> 00:37:08,490
Whether you're awake or asleep, watch out for fire.

539
00:37:09,120 --> 00:37:11,860
Right, be careful with fire. Be careful.

540
00:37:19,630 --> 00:37:22,770
Why isn't my hair working today?

541
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:26,670
Don't tell me you still have feelings for her.

542
00:37:27,310 --> 00:37:28,310
What?

543
00:37:28,410 --> 00:37:30,080
I mean, you're going to see your ex-wife.

544
00:37:30,140 --> 00:37:31,680
Why are you putting in so much effort?

545
00:37:31,780 --> 00:37:33,650
No, Ha Neul said he wanted to see his mom at work,

546
00:37:33,710 --> 00:37:34,720
so I'm taking him.

547
00:37:35,950 --> 00:37:36,950
But you never know, right?

548
00:37:37,450 --> 00:37:40,120
I might run into someone from the film industry.

549
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:43,720
And then if I get a chance, my screenplay...

550
00:37:44,430 --> 00:37:47,060
Anyway, you know how important first impressions are.

551
00:37:47,600 --> 00:37:49,660
Are you going to Ha Neul's mom's film company now?

552
00:37:50,670 --> 00:37:51,670
Yes.

553
00:37:53,300 --> 00:37:54,470
But Mom, where are you going?

554
00:37:54,600 --> 00:37:56,070
I'm going tiger hunting.

555
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:07,380
Now that the participants for the senior event are all set,

556
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:09,580
I guess we can start working.

557
00:38:11,020 --> 00:38:13,250
I'm counting on you. Do a great job.

558
00:38:13,590 --> 00:38:15,860
It's no trouble. I'm getting paid for it, after all.

559
00:38:18,490 --> 00:38:20,730
By the way, from now on, for this kind of work,

560
00:38:21,230 --> 00:38:23,130
I'd appreciate it if you sent a staff member instead.

561
00:38:23,830 --> 00:38:25,600
After all, you're the CEO of a hotel.

562
00:38:26,070 --> 00:38:27,900
Running around for a single document like this,

563
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:29,040
don't you think that's a bit much?

564
00:38:30,170 --> 00:38:31,510
You're right. I'll do that from now on.

565
00:38:32,940 --> 00:38:35,110
But I came today because I had something...

566
00:38:35,180 --> 00:38:36,380
to give you in person.

567
00:38:45,220 --> 00:38:46,220
Is this...

568
00:38:47,420 --> 00:38:48,420
That's right.

569
00:38:49,390 --> 00:38:52,560
It's the ring your mother gave me before she passed.

570
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:57,830
It was a precious ring she gave me, asking me to take good care of you.

571
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,370
I missed my chance to return it,

572
00:39:00,430 --> 00:39:02,100
and I've been holding onto it all this time.

573
00:39:04,910 --> 00:39:05,910
But at least for today,

574
00:39:06,740 --> 00:39:08,840
I knew I had to give it back to you.

575
00:39:10,210 --> 00:39:11,210
Today...

576
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,950
It's the anniversary of your parents' death.

577
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:23,890
You remembered that?

578
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:26,890
I've never forgotten, not even for a moment.

579
00:39:31,400 --> 00:39:33,630
You have a visitor.

580
00:39:34,170 --> 00:39:35,540
Should I come back later?

581
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:36,740
Oh, no, that's all right.

582
00:39:37,810 --> 00:39:38,810
Well, I'll be going then.

583
00:39:43,540 --> 00:39:45,650
Oh, fancy seeing you here.

584
00:39:46,910 --> 00:39:47,920
Oh, yes.

585
00:39:49,050 --> 00:39:50,050
Hello.

586
00:39:50,120 --> 00:39:51,550
Yes, hello.

587
00:39:58,490 --> 00:39:59,490
Wait.

588
00:40:00,490 --> 00:40:03,630
- That man just now... - Excuse me, Lawyer, one moment.

589
00:40:11,810 --> 00:40:12,810
Wait a second.

590
00:40:15,740 --> 00:40:16,740
Take this with you.

591
00:40:19,750 --> 00:40:22,750
My mom gave this to you, so you should keep it.

592
00:40:24,190 --> 00:40:25,190
And...

593
00:40:26,020 --> 00:40:28,160
thank you for remembering the anniversary.

594
00:40:28,390 --> 00:40:29,790
(J&White)

595
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:39,800
Nothing is going on between those two, right?

596
00:40:39,870 --> 00:40:41,500
I'm just overthinking this, right?

597
00:40:42,140 --> 00:40:44,140
You're writing a romance novel over here.

598
00:40:46,910 --> 00:40:48,540
Why are you asking me?

599
00:40:49,140 --> 00:40:50,140
If you're that curious,

600
00:40:50,210 --> 00:40:51,810
there's a fortune-teller at the intersection up ahead.

601
00:40:51,880 --> 00:40:52,880
Go ask them.

602
00:40:55,080 --> 00:40:57,250
How do you expect to get a divorce, acting like this?

603
00:40:58,250 --> 00:41:00,620
My wife used to absolutely hate that jerk.

604
00:41:00,890 --> 00:41:03,120
But today, something felt different.

605
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:07,330
The vibe between them was definitely different than usual.

606
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:09,830
If you're that worried about it,

607
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:13,070
you should write her a love letter, not a legal response.

608
00:41:13,600 --> 00:41:14,900
At least that would be more honest.

609
00:41:19,510 --> 00:41:22,280
- Excuse me a moment. - Go ahead.

610
00:41:24,350 --> 00:41:25,350
What is it?

611
00:41:26,510 --> 00:41:28,650
I'm in a meeting with my lawyer. What's wrong?

612
00:41:30,820 --> 00:41:33,090
Another woman? What are you talking about?

613
00:41:33,450 --> 00:41:34,420
No, it's nothing like that.

614
00:41:34,490 --> 00:41:35,920
Why would Seung Ho say something so ridiculous?

615
00:41:37,020 --> 00:41:39,690
I don't know. I'm busy. I'll call you back.

616
00:41:41,300 --> 00:41:42,300
Jeez.

617
00:41:42,930 --> 00:41:44,500
Who was that, for you to answer the phone like that?

618
00:41:45,030 --> 00:41:46,030
Just a debt collector.

619
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:48,970
So, where were we?

620
00:41:51,140 --> 00:41:54,580
Excuse me, are you Bae Su Ji, the lawyer?

621
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:56,780
Yes.

622
00:41:57,140 --> 00:41:59,510
So you're Bae Su Ji? You crazy witch.

623
00:41:59,610 --> 00:42:02,280
Hey, get over here. Who do you think you're seducing, you little tramp?

624
00:42:02,350 --> 00:42:03,880
Why are you hitting on my son?

625
00:42:04,250 --> 00:42:05,250
It's my mom.

626
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:07,520
What did you say? You little...

627
00:42:08,120 --> 00:42:12,190
- How dare you hit on my son? - Mom, what are you doing?

628
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:14,660
You crazy fool. You jerk.

629
00:42:14,730 --> 00:42:17,400
Did you really pick your lawyer based on their looks?

630
00:42:18,130 --> 00:42:19,770
Ma'am, please calm down.

631
00:42:19,870 --> 00:42:21,440
Get off me. You pathetic fool, did you run out on...

632
00:42:21,500 --> 00:42:23,200
your family just to fool around with this young thing?

633
00:42:23,300 --> 00:42:24,410
Is that why you ran away from home?

634
00:42:24,570 --> 00:42:25,570
Mom.

635
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:28,580
You jerk. You absolute jerk.

636
00:42:29,040 --> 00:42:30,950
Stop right there.

637
00:42:31,750 --> 00:42:33,410
That actually hurts.

638
00:42:36,850 --> 00:42:38,650
Ryu Mi Soon.

639
00:42:40,120 --> 00:42:41,660
How have you not changed one bit?

640
00:42:44,090 --> 00:42:45,090
Su Ji?

641
00:42:52,430 --> 00:42:53,430
Let's go.

642
00:42:56,100 --> 00:42:57,270
How can I help you?

643
00:42:57,640 --> 00:43:00,010
Yes, I'm here to see Director Song Woo Young.

644
00:43:00,370 --> 00:43:01,940
We have an appointment to meet at two o'clock.

645
00:43:02,240 --> 00:43:04,110
And you are...

646
00:43:04,450 --> 00:43:07,050
I'm the father of the director's son.

647
00:43:07,480 --> 00:43:08,650
And this is her son.

648
00:43:08,950 --> 00:43:10,680
Ha Neul, what are you doing? Go on and say hello.

649
00:43:10,850 --> 00:43:12,020
Hello.

650
00:43:12,390 --> 00:43:14,290
- Please wait a moment. - Okay.

651
00:43:26,070 --> 00:43:27,070
Yes.

652
00:43:33,470 --> 00:43:36,010
Ha Neul, it looks like your mom's very busy.

653
00:43:36,540 --> 00:43:37,540
Let's come back later.

654
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:44,150
(Bae Su Ji Law Office)

655
00:43:54,230 --> 00:43:56,360
But Mom, how did you find this place anyway?

656
00:43:56,700 --> 00:43:58,500
Oh, please. How do you think?

657
00:43:59,170 --> 00:44:01,700
I saw the business card in your motel room, of course.

658
00:44:03,540 --> 00:44:05,440
But I had no idea that Bae Su Ji was him.

659
00:44:06,070 --> 00:44:07,370
I never would have dreamed it.

660
00:44:07,640 --> 00:44:09,380
Whether you knew it was me or not,

661
00:44:10,710 --> 00:44:12,980
that was still out of line.

662
00:44:14,280 --> 00:44:17,550
Wait, so are you saying you two are friends from back home?

663
00:44:18,290 --> 00:44:20,650
Yes, Father Kwon and us.

664
00:44:21,420 --> 00:44:24,430
The three of us have been friends since we were kids.

665
00:44:26,990 --> 00:44:29,430
Anyway, Su Ji, it's so good to see you.

666
00:44:30,230 --> 00:44:33,330
I'd heard bits and pieces about you now and then,

667
00:44:33,530 --> 00:44:35,770
but I had no idea you were so close by.

668
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:38,070
I'll be sure to come by often, Su Ji.

669
00:44:38,310 --> 00:44:40,470
No, you really don't have to do that.

670
00:44:40,610 --> 00:44:42,780
Seeing you this one time is more than enough.

671
00:44:42,940 --> 00:44:47,780
What do you mean, one time? Su Ji, are you eating properly?

672
00:44:48,680 --> 00:44:51,520
You look even paler than you did when you were young.

673
00:44:53,090 --> 00:44:55,120
I'll have to bring you some side dishes.

674
00:45:01,230 --> 00:45:03,760
Mom, let's go. My consultation time is up for today. Let's go.

675
00:45:04,060 --> 00:45:05,870
- Su Ji, do you like braised beef? - Let's go.

676
00:45:05,970 --> 00:45:06,970
What about pickled wild garlic?

677
00:45:07,600 --> 00:45:10,040
I have some delicious seasoned vegetables at home.

678
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:11,770
I'll be back, Su Ji.

679
00:45:26,090 --> 00:45:27,120
Mom, Dad.

680
00:45:29,120 --> 00:45:30,120
Have you been well?

681
00:45:30,390 --> 00:45:32,530
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

682
00:45:32,590 --> 00:45:34,860
Life got so busy. It's been too long, hasn't it?

683
00:45:36,300 --> 00:45:37,300
I'm sorry.

684
00:45:41,140 --> 00:45:42,500
It's not like I was doing anything that important.

685
00:45:47,140 --> 00:45:48,640
Your only daughter...

686
00:45:50,580 --> 00:45:51,580
has been...

687
00:45:52,780 --> 00:45:54,920
I was so focused on my own struggles that I neglected you.

688
00:45:55,450 --> 00:45:57,420
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

689
00:45:57,480 --> 00:46:00,820
Mom, Dad, you remember Calvin, don't you?

690
00:46:03,920 --> 00:46:04,930
Calvin,

691
00:46:06,090 --> 00:46:08,360
he's the one who told me today was the anniversary of your passing.

692
00:46:13,400 --> 00:46:15,140
The anniversary that even I had forgotten,

693
00:46:16,800 --> 00:46:18,310
Calvin remembered.

694
00:46:18,410 --> 00:46:21,480
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

695
00:46:24,550 --> 00:46:26,680
I should have lived a better life.

696
00:46:30,750 --> 00:46:31,750
I'm sorry.

697
00:46:32,920 --> 00:46:34,120
I'm sorry, Dad.

698
00:46:46,500 --> 00:46:50,270
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

699
00:47:07,520 --> 00:47:10,690
One of my employees made a huge mistake.

700
00:47:11,430 --> 00:47:14,630
While organising the dress list for the senior wedding couples,

701
00:47:15,360 --> 00:47:18,100
they must have mixed up two clients with the same name.

702
00:47:18,600 --> 00:47:21,500
The dress designs and measurements got swapped,

703
00:47:22,940 --> 00:47:25,470
so it looks like we'll have to remake them.

704
00:47:27,870 --> 00:47:29,010
Oh, I see.

705
00:47:30,340 --> 00:47:33,010
Does that mean you have to postpone the wedding?

706
00:47:33,550 --> 00:47:34,850
That would be ideal, but...

707
00:47:35,420 --> 00:47:37,880
the wedding date has already been announced.

708
00:47:38,820 --> 00:47:39,920
Don't worry about that.

709
00:47:40,450 --> 00:47:41,760
I'll take care of it.

710
00:47:42,490 --> 00:47:44,120
I'm sorry to cause you trouble.

711
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:47,490
Not at all. Mistakes happen at work.

712
00:47:49,900 --> 00:47:52,330
Don't worry too much about it. It's not a big deal.

713
00:47:53,270 --> 00:47:54,570
I can make any adjustments you need.

714
00:47:58,740 --> 00:47:59,740
Pretending you agree when you don't, pretending you like things you hate,

715
00:47:59,810 --> 00:48:00,810
sucking up to people,

716
00:48:00,870 --> 00:48:03,040
and acting like a phony.

717
00:48:03,780 --> 00:48:04,850
What's that if not a clown?

718
00:48:05,780 --> 00:48:07,180
I don't want to stoop to that level.

719
00:48:07,550 --> 00:48:10,480
So, you refuse to change the design no matter what, is that it?

720
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:12,690
I'm absolutely not changing it.

721
00:48:12,990 --> 00:48:15,390
Not without a request from Man Ju. Not even if the sky falls.

722
00:48:18,030 --> 00:48:19,960
- Mi Young. - Yes?

723
00:48:20,130 --> 00:48:21,500
Since you're here, would you like...

724
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:23,330
to see the wedding hall construction site?

725
00:48:24,260 --> 00:48:25,270
A wedding hall?

726
00:48:25,700 --> 00:48:28,240
We're building a wedding hall for our own brand.

727
00:48:28,870 --> 00:48:29,870
Calvin Wedding Hall.

728
00:48:30,470 --> 00:48:32,340
The interior isn't even done,

729
00:48:32,710 --> 00:48:34,240
and it's still in the very early stages.

730
00:48:35,510 --> 00:48:37,310
So I was hoping you could take a look...

731
00:48:37,380 --> 00:48:38,950
and give me some good feedback.

732
00:48:40,410 --> 00:48:42,020
Why is my opinion that important?

733
00:48:43,280 --> 00:48:44,350
Because it's your opinion.

734
00:48:45,990 --> 00:48:47,290
If you give me any feedback at all,

735
00:48:47,750 --> 00:48:49,560
it would be a huge help to me.

736
00:48:51,260 --> 00:48:52,260
Would you?

737
00:49:18,090 --> 00:49:19,090
Take a look over there.

738
00:49:21,620 --> 00:49:24,460
- So that's the indoor wedding hall? - That's right.

739
00:49:26,230 --> 00:49:27,930
Where will the seating be arranged?

740
00:49:27,990 --> 00:49:30,060
Wait a minute. Ms. Park.

741
00:49:30,430 --> 00:49:31,430
Ah, yes.

742
00:49:32,900 --> 00:49:34,670
Let's hear what CEO Baek has to say.

743
00:49:35,040 --> 00:49:36,800
Yes.

744
00:49:37,940 --> 00:49:42,810
I want the flowers to connect to the stage.

745
00:49:46,810 --> 00:49:48,620
And if the seating is arranged this way,

746
00:49:48,680 --> 00:49:50,180
is the entrance over there?

747
00:50:00,860 --> 00:50:02,060
Thanks for today, Mi Young.

748
00:50:02,830 --> 00:50:03,830
Don't mention it.

749
00:50:04,030 --> 00:50:06,500
Anyway, I'll have the dresses made as soon as possible...

750
00:50:06,730 --> 00:50:08,600
so there are no delays with the wedding schedule.

751
00:50:09,140 --> 00:50:10,140
Thanks.

752
00:50:13,270 --> 00:50:14,270
You should get going.

753
00:50:14,740 --> 00:50:17,540
Oh, okay. Take care.

754
00:50:30,590 --> 00:50:32,430
Well, isn't this a sight?

755
00:50:34,530 --> 00:50:36,760
Now you're just flaunting your little romance in public.

756
00:50:38,130 --> 00:50:39,130
What?

757
00:50:39,230 --> 00:50:40,230
It's still work hours.

758
00:50:40,300 --> 00:50:41,700
Don't you think you're going too far?

759
00:50:41,770 --> 00:50:43,170
There are other people watching.

760
00:50:43,370 --> 00:50:44,470
People watching?

761
00:50:46,170 --> 00:50:48,180
Do you really have the right to say that to me?

762
00:50:48,510 --> 00:50:49,510
What about me?

763
00:50:49,610 --> 00:50:52,350
Have I ever once slacked off during work hours?

764
00:50:52,610 --> 00:50:56,380
So you did that because it wasn't during work hours?

765
00:50:56,750 --> 00:50:57,750
"That?"

766
00:50:57,880 --> 00:51:00,490
What do you call spending the night in a motel with another woman?

767
00:51:00,750 --> 00:51:02,160
Hey, how many times do I have to tell you...

768
00:51:02,220 --> 00:51:03,220
it was a misunderstanding?

769
00:51:03,360 --> 00:51:07,160
I saw it with my own two eyes, so what is there to misunderstand?

770
00:51:07,360 --> 00:51:10,160
Fine. Then keep thinking that.

771
00:51:13,330 --> 00:51:15,070
And where are you going during work hours?

772
00:51:15,340 --> 00:51:16,440
I'm going to get food.

773
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:18,840
Because I've been working so hard I haven't even eaten.

774
00:51:23,680 --> 00:51:24,680
Unbelievable.

775
00:51:25,250 --> 00:51:27,380
That's not strong enough.

776
00:51:28,350 --> 00:51:31,420
If there had been some PDA, it might be a different story.

777
00:51:32,890 --> 00:51:35,060
Just the fact that they came out of a motel together...

778
00:51:36,090 --> 00:51:38,160
doesn't carry much weight legally.

779
00:51:40,190 --> 00:51:41,190
I see.

780
00:51:41,530 --> 00:51:43,100
But now that we have a reason to be suspicious,

781
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:44,630
it's worth keeping a close eye on them,

782
00:51:44,700 --> 00:51:45,700
don't you think?

783
00:51:51,100 --> 00:51:54,070
How do you and Calvin know each other?

784
00:51:54,740 --> 00:51:55,740
What?

785
00:51:56,410 --> 00:51:57,510
A little while ago,

786
00:51:58,410 --> 00:51:59,410
at the office.

787
00:52:00,280 --> 00:52:02,120
Oh, that's...

788
00:52:03,450 --> 00:52:06,520
We're collaborating on a project for work.

789
00:52:06,850 --> 00:52:09,420
So that's what it is.

790
00:52:10,590 --> 00:52:12,390
Then, as for you, a lawyer,

791
00:52:13,330 --> 00:52:15,030
how do you know him?

792
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:17,200
Calvin...

793
00:52:17,900 --> 00:52:19,470
was my client.

794
00:52:19,900 --> 00:52:23,140
I handled his divorce.

795
00:52:24,100 --> 00:52:25,110
I see.

796
00:52:25,840 --> 00:52:26,970
You and Calvin...

797
00:52:27,510 --> 00:52:28,640
Is something going on between you two?

798
00:52:30,710 --> 00:52:31,710
It's just...

799
00:52:32,480 --> 00:52:33,850
a lawyer's intuition, shall we say.

800
00:52:37,620 --> 00:52:38,690
Before I got married,

801
00:52:39,720 --> 00:52:41,590
we used to date.

802
00:52:42,720 --> 00:52:43,760
Don't tell me...

803
00:52:44,460 --> 00:52:47,260
you were Calvin's first love?

804
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:52,370
What are the odds of us meeting like this?

805
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:57,500
That's all in the past now.

806
00:52:57,740 --> 00:53:00,310
To say it's all in the past,

807
00:53:01,610 --> 00:53:03,910
isn't this a little too shocking?

808
00:53:04,840 --> 00:53:05,850
What?

809
00:53:06,110 --> 00:53:07,110
By any chance,

810
00:53:07,810 --> 00:53:10,620
do you know why Calvin got divorced? Or rather,

811
00:53:11,350 --> 00:53:13,020
why he got married...

812
00:53:14,320 --> 00:53:15,290
in the first place?

813
00:53:16,060 --> 00:53:18,960
The woman he was secretly seeing at the time...

814
00:53:19,860 --> 00:53:21,130
got pregnant.

815
00:53:22,060 --> 00:53:23,330
I figured you wouldn't know.

816
00:53:24,500 --> 00:53:25,500
To be honest,

817
00:53:25,700 --> 00:53:29,070
it's a pretty well-known story among those in the know.

818
00:53:31,070 --> 00:53:32,270
Seven years ago,

819
00:53:33,410 --> 00:53:35,080
Calvin and his half-brothers...

820
00:53:36,280 --> 00:53:38,180
apparently had a dispute over control of the company.

821
00:53:38,510 --> 00:53:39,510
Yes.

822
00:53:42,150 --> 00:53:43,780
You've had a tough time, haven't you?

823
00:53:44,220 --> 00:53:45,720
Let's just relax and eat today.

824
00:53:46,150 --> 00:53:47,820
The very day he went to his family's home...

825
00:53:47,890 --> 00:53:49,320
to make up with his half-brothers...

826
00:53:50,160 --> 00:53:51,160
Cheers.

827
00:53:51,220 --> 00:53:53,730
- Cheers. - That's when it all happened.

828
00:53:54,090 --> 00:53:56,130
- This is nice, right? - What do you want to eat? Cake?

829
00:53:56,200 --> 00:53:58,330
- It'll be fine. - You can't get drunk.

830
00:53:58,400 --> 00:54:00,930
- It's fine, it's fine. - Let's have another drink.

831
00:54:14,650 --> 00:54:16,780
I'm... I'm fine.

832
00:54:35,940 --> 00:54:37,200
His half-brothers...

833
00:54:38,200 --> 00:54:41,040
intentionally set a trap for Calvin,

834
00:54:43,980 --> 00:54:45,510
and he fell for it,

835
00:54:45,910 --> 00:54:47,850
ending up marrying that woman.

836
00:54:55,160 --> 00:54:58,730
His brothers said if he just gave up his management rights,

837
00:54:59,190 --> 00:55:01,530
they would cover everything up.

838
00:55:02,430 --> 00:55:05,830
But apparently, he refused.

839
00:55:08,170 --> 00:55:12,540
The entire family was caught up in a soap opera of epic proportions.

840
00:55:14,610 --> 00:55:15,610
And...

841
00:55:16,810 --> 00:55:18,680
the biggest victim in that whole drama...

842
00:55:19,380 --> 00:55:20,980
is sitting right in front of me.

843
00:55:36,230 --> 00:55:37,230
CEO Ji.

844
00:55:37,930 --> 00:55:39,100
Where are you going?

845
00:55:40,800 --> 00:55:41,940
Stop.

846
00:55:46,570 --> 00:55:47,710
What the?

847
00:55:50,810 --> 00:55:53,480
- Stop. - Why are you running away?

848
00:55:54,410 --> 00:55:55,750
Let's do this.

849
00:55:55,850 --> 00:55:58,690
That thing we agreed on, about meeting three times.

850
00:56:00,190 --> 00:56:01,790
Let's just call it off.

851
00:56:02,420 --> 00:56:03,420
What?

852
00:56:03,520 --> 00:56:04,690
I am really sorry,

853
00:56:04,820 --> 00:56:07,190
but I am just not in a position to do that right now.

854
00:56:08,260 --> 00:56:10,130
Then you should have just said so.

855
00:56:10,630 --> 00:56:12,230
Why are you making a fool out of me?

856
00:56:13,400 --> 00:56:14,400
Is it perhaps...

857
00:56:14,870 --> 00:56:16,170
because of your wife?

858
00:56:19,110 --> 00:56:22,480
No, that is just a misunderstanding. Nothing happened between us.

859
00:56:22,880 --> 00:56:25,480
Still, she saw us together at the motel,

860
00:56:25,980 --> 00:56:27,010
so it's understandable she misunderstood.

861
00:56:28,080 --> 00:56:29,920
If that is how you feel,

862
00:56:30,650 --> 00:56:31,850
there is nothing I can do.

863
00:56:37,590 --> 00:56:40,060
Actually, before I go,

864
00:56:40,690 --> 00:56:42,200
mind if I create a little misunderstanding of my own?

865
00:56:42,660 --> 00:56:44,530
Create a misunderstanding?

866
00:56:45,030 --> 00:56:46,230
Because I saw something too.

867
00:56:51,700 --> 00:56:53,910
What kind of misunderstanding are you talking about?

868
00:57:13,530 --> 00:57:14,530
Mi Young.

869
00:57:15,330 --> 00:57:16,330
Yes?

870
00:57:16,600 --> 00:57:18,300
What's wrong? Is it not good?

871
00:57:19,500 --> 00:57:20,630
Oh, no.

872
00:57:22,570 --> 00:57:23,570
So what is going on?

873
00:57:24,100 --> 00:57:26,570
It is not like you to ask me to dinner.

874
00:57:41,890 --> 00:57:43,190
Why didn't you tell me?

875
00:57:44,120 --> 00:57:46,990
What didn't I tell you?

876
00:57:49,230 --> 00:57:50,930
The day you went to see your half-brothers.

877
00:57:52,530 --> 00:57:53,800
When you went to your family's home.

878
00:57:56,300 --> 00:57:57,370
You will be fine, right?

879
00:57:58,240 --> 00:58:00,340
If your brothers ask you questions, answer them well.

880
00:58:01,070 --> 00:58:03,540
And try to laugh at their jokes, even if they are not funny.

881
00:58:04,280 --> 00:58:06,680
You look angry when you are quiet.

882
00:58:07,180 --> 00:58:09,080
They do not care about things like that.

883
00:58:09,680 --> 00:58:10,980
They do not even like me that much.

884
00:58:11,180 --> 00:58:12,820
But they are still family.

885
00:58:13,490 --> 00:58:15,290
Deep down, your brothers might have been...

886
00:58:15,390 --> 00:58:16,860
hoping you would reach out first.

887
00:58:17,390 --> 00:58:19,030
If you approach them first,

888
00:58:19,190 --> 00:58:21,490
they will welcome you with open arms.

889
00:58:21,930 --> 00:58:24,500
Look at you, Mi Young. You are all grown up.

890
00:58:24,730 --> 00:58:25,830
Hey, I'm older than you.

891
00:58:32,840 --> 00:58:34,110
I will do my best.

892
00:58:36,380 --> 00:58:37,380
I love you.

893
00:58:38,110 --> 00:58:39,110
Me too.

894
00:58:39,580 --> 00:58:41,780
- Go get them. - Go get them.

895
00:58:43,820 --> 00:58:44,820
That day,

896
00:58:45,790 --> 00:58:48,050
something so terrible happened.

897
00:58:49,590 --> 00:58:50,760
Why didn't you tell me?

898
00:58:52,460 --> 00:58:55,360
Is that why you broke up with me?

899
00:58:57,930 --> 00:59:00,000
Because you were scared of your brothers' threats?

900
00:59:00,500 --> 00:59:01,500
Or...

901
00:59:02,640 --> 00:59:06,210
because you just could not give up management of the Calvin Hotel?

902
00:59:08,370 --> 00:59:09,880
I could give up everything else,

903
00:59:12,110 --> 00:59:13,850
but I could not give up that child.

904
00:59:16,950 --> 00:59:18,820
The child that woman was carrying at the time...

905
00:59:20,950 --> 00:59:21,990
I could not...

906
00:59:25,190 --> 00:59:26,690
let that child be born illegitimate like me.

907
00:59:28,390 --> 00:59:29,600
So that is why you got a divorce?

908
00:59:30,830 --> 00:59:31,830
Because that child...

909
00:59:34,570 --> 00:59:36,470
turned out not to be yours?

910
00:59:38,300 --> 00:59:39,310
Mi Young.

911
00:59:42,380 --> 00:59:43,380
All this time...

912
00:59:44,910 --> 00:59:47,250
All this time, I hated you so much.

913
01:00:41,500 --> 01:00:44,470
(Epilogue)

914
01:00:46,540 --> 01:00:47,540
Hey, Calvin.

915
01:01:09,630 --> 01:01:12,600
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

916
01:01:14,330 --> 01:01:16,640
- What is this? - I just changed my mind.

917
01:01:16,970 --> 01:01:20,070
This is what we call a classic backstab.

918
01:01:21,610 --> 01:01:24,280
- That psycho. - This operation's code name is...

919
01:01:24,340 --> 01:01:25,340
To that place.

920
01:01:26,480 --> 01:01:29,020
I have seen it all now.

921
01:01:29,520 --> 01:01:30,520
A drink...

922
01:01:30,580 --> 01:01:32,350
To think he would bring a woman into our home.

923
01:01:32,450 --> 01:01:33,850
I mean, is he out of his mind?

924
01:01:35,590 --> 01:01:37,820
If you're jealous, go ahead and bring someone over.

925
01:01:39,490 --> 01:01:41,160
You keep bringing up old wounds...

926
01:01:41,230 --> 01:01:42,460
and blaming other people. Please,

927
01:01:42,530 --> 01:01:43,860
just break that nasty habit of yours.

928
01:01:44,730 --> 01:01:46,230
Please, just shut up.
